  "goodToKnow": "Hauptamtlich means full-time and paid, as one's main job: ein hauptamtlicher Bürgermeister, hauptamtliche Mitarbeiter of a club or party. The opposite is ehrenamtlich (voluntary) and nebenamtlich (part-time, alongside a main job). Most of Germany's fire brigades are Freiwillige Feuerwehren with about a million volunteers; only large cities have a hauptamtliche Berufsfeuerwehr."
